      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/man-la-yahduruhu-al-faqih:4:175:141",
      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/1/175/5906",
      "text": [
        " : \"هَبَطَ جَبْرَئِيلُ عَلَى آدَمَ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ فَقَالَ يَا آدَمُ إِنِّي أُمِرْتُ أَنْ أُخَيِّرَكَ وَاحِدَةً مِنْ ثَلاَثٍ فَاخْتَرْ وَاحِدَةً وَ دَعْ اِثْنَتَيْنِ فَقَالَ لَهُ وَ مَا تِلْكَ اَلثَّلاَثُ قَالَ اَلْعَقْلُ وَ اَلْحَيَاءُ وَ اَلدِّينُ فَقَالَ آدَمُ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ فَإِنِّي قَدِ اِخْتَرْتُ اَلْعَقْلَ فَقَالَ جَبْرَئِيلُ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ لِلْحَيَاءِ وَ اَلدِّينِ اِنْصَرِفَا وَ دَعَاهُ فَقَالاَ يَا جَبْرَئِيلُ إِنَّا أُمِرْنَا أَنْ نَكُونَ مَعَ اَلْعَقْلِ حَيْثُ كَانَ قَالَ فَشَأْنَكُمَا وَ عَرَجَ \"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5906 - It is narrated from Abu Jameelah Al-Mufaddal ibn Salih, from Sa'd ibn Tarif, from Al-Asbagh ibn Nubata, from Commander of the Faithful Imam Ali ibn Abi Talib (as) who said:\n\"Jibril (as) descended upon Adam (as) and said: 'O' Adam, I have been commanded to offer you a choice among three things, so choose one and leave the other two.'\nAdam (as) asked: 'What are those three things?'\nJibril (as) replied: 'Intellect, modesty, and religion.'\nAdam (as) said: 'I choose intellect.'\nSo Jibril (as) said to modesty and religion: 'Depart from him.'\nThey both replied: 'O' Jibril, we have been commanded to remain with intellect wherever it is.'\nJibril (as) said: 'Then it is your affair,' and he ascended.\""
        ]
      }
    },
